"Dissociation of the combustion products of octane at 3000 K and 100 bar"

"Octane C8H18 burns with 20 % excess dry air: C8H18 + 12.5 (1 + 0.2) (O2 + 3.76 N2). The products are in chemical
equilibrium at T and P, in the gas phase: the procedure CHEM_EQUIL returns the mole fractions of the 14 species
H2, O2, H2O, CO, CO2, OH, H, O, N2, N, NO, NO2, CH4 and Ar from the ratios of the atoms of argon, carbon, hydrogen and
nitrogen to the oxygen atoms (A\O, C\O, H\O, N\O). Units of the model: T in C, P in Pa (the EES files pass K and kPa).
The thermodynamic data are the NASA-Glenn polynomials of the 14 species; EES's older data give the same major species
within 1 % (x_CO2 = 0.08724803022 at this state) and OH, NO, NO2 and H2 a few percent apart."

T_K = 3000 [K]
T = T_K - 273.15 [C]
P = 1E7 [Pa]

"Atoms per oxygen atom of C8H18 + 12.5 (1 + e) (O2 + 3.76 N2), e = 0.2"
e = 0.2
a = 12.5*(1 + e)                         "kmol of O2 per kmol of fuel"
A\O = 0                                  "no argon"
C\O = 8/(2*a)
H\O = 18/(2*a)
N\O = 3.76

CALL CHEM_EQUIL(P, T, A\O, C\O, H\O, N\O : x_H2, x_O2, x_H2O, x_CO, x_CO2, x_OH, x_H, x_O, x_N2, x_N, x_NO, x_NO2, x_CH4, x_Ar)

"Check of the mole fractions"
sum_x = x_H2 + x_O2 + x_H2O + x_CO + x_CO2 + x_OH + x_H + x_O + x_N2 + x_N + x_NO + x_NO2 + x_CH4 + x_Ar

"Degree of dissociation of the carbon: the part of it that is CO"
CO_share = x_CO/(x_CO + x_CO2)
